{
  "quest.460216B38525C483.quest_desc": [
    "Four guardians, four pieces of armor.",
    "",
    "Craft the &aBattlemage Armor&r. Each piece takes gold, obsidian, a colored rune and one essence: Water for the boots, Earth for the chestplate, Air for the helmet and Fire for the leggings.",
  ],
  "quest.5032BB5B2E4CEC4A.quest_desc": [
    "A fresh table gives a spell two shape groups. Each upgrade adds one more, up to five.",
    "",
    "Craft the three &aInscription Table Upgrades&r and apply them in order by right-clicking the table. A table keeps its tier when you break it.",
    "",
    "Shape groups let one spell carry several ways of delivering the same effect. A Heal spell with Self in one group and Projectile in another can heal you or a friend.",
  ],
  "quest.234EDABC4DC710EC.quest_desc": [
    "Only a ritual built high in the sky calls the Air Guardian.",
    "",
    "Summon and defeat the &cAir Guardian&r. Build a &2Gold Inlay&r ring at Y 128 or higher in the Overworld and drop a &aTarma Root&r in the center.",
    "",
    "Arrows and other projectiles do nothing to it and it takes no fall damage, so fight it with spells; lightning hurts it most. It drops the &2Air Sled&r, a mount that flies.",
  ],
  "quest.3ED3881C36561AFA.quest_desc": [
    "Every spell part has to be learned before you can use it, and the &aOcculus&r is where you learn them. Craft and place an &aOcculus&r.",
    "",
    "It opens four skill trees: Offense, Defense, Utility and Talents. Each part costs one blue, green, or red skill point, and a part's parents have to be learned first.",
    "",
    "Your 3 starting points buy exactly the first spell the Compendium suggests: &2Projectile&r from Offense, then &aTouch&r and Dig from Utility.",
  ],
  "quest.5CDB81EABD6385D0.quest_desc": [
    "Bigger spell parts ask the altar for Etherium as well as items. Area of Effect, Wall, Zone, and the contingencies all need it.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aObelisk&r and a &2Crystal Wrench&r. Fuel the obelisk, then right-click it with the wrench and then click the &2Altar Core&r to link them. With the altar's lever on, it draws Etherium while it crafts.",
    "",
    "Each generator holds 5000 Etherium, and one altar can draw from several generators.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each fuel gives a set amount of Etherium.",
    "",
    "- &aVinteum Dust&r: 200 Etherium.",
    "- &2Block of Vinteum&r: 1800 Etherium.",
    "- &aLiquid Etherium Bucket&r: 2000 Etherium.",
    "",
    "Those are base amounts. A ring of &2Wizard's Chalk&r around the obelisk doubles them, and four pillars on top of that triples them.",
    "",
    "Each pillar stands on a corner of a 5x5 square centered on the obelisk, with two &2Stone Bricks&r under a &aChiseled Stone Brick&r. Everything else in that 5x5, 3 block high space has to be air.",
  ],
  "quest.3070FD15982582F5.title": "The Arcane Compendium",
  "quest.5CDB81EABD6385D0.title": "Etherium",
  "quest.7C03B317E26A290C.quest_desc": [
    "Build it like a snow golem and the Ice Guardian answers instead.",
    "",
    "Summon and defeat the &cIce Guardian&r. In a cold Overworld biome, lay an &2Iron Inlay&r ring, stack two &aSnow Blocks&r in its center and place a Carved Pumpkin on top, last.",
    "",
    "Fire hurts it most and freezing does nothing. It drops &2Winter's Grasp&r, a weapon that freezes what it hits and pulls enemies in when thrown.",
  ],
  "task.444799D362DAFEE9.title": "&eObserve&r: &dCelestial Prism",
  "quest.5B7AE500196A3035.title": "Sunstone",
  "quest.1FF93FE18E8F7EE4.title": "Affinity Tomes",
  "quest.6F50BE9EBF4E149D.title": "The Crafting Altar",
  "quest.5B7AE500196A3035.quest_desc": [
    "Sunstone forms in the Nether, and only right beside lava.",
    "",
    "Mine &aSunstone&r. It replaces Nether stone that touches a lava source between Y 31 and 33, so search the shores of lava lakes at that height.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: This block is not lava-proof.",
  ],
  "quest.5E3BBD0F8D9946E3.title": "Forgotten Magic",
  "quest.1A850EA969AFE13C.title": "&dBlack Aurem",
  "quest.43B8B4ADA8187922.title": "Arcane Minerals",
  "quest.5032BB5B2E4CEC4A.title": "Shape Groups",
  "quest.1F694D7302EBE072.title": "Your First Spell",
  "quest.2A0AC5FFA464150C.title": "Water Guardian",
  "quest.45CD833DF80BEAC3.quest_desc": [
    "Every cast costs mana and adds burnout. Run short of either and the spell fails.",
    "",
    "Bake a &aMana Cake&r for a long boost to Mana Regeneration. A &2Mana Martini&r lowers burnout for a while, and mana potions come in six strengths; JEI lists them all.",
    "",
    "Your mana pool grows by 50 with every magic level, so leveling is the long-term answer.",
  ],
  "quest.6F50BE9EBF4E149D.quest_desc": [
    "Spells aren't crafted on a table. They're assembled at a structure that takes your ingredients one at a time.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aAltar Core&r and six &2Magic Walls&r, then build the &3Crafting Altar&r. The render above this quest shows a finished one, and the next pages cover the rules.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The altar checks its shape once a second. When it forms, the core takes on the look of your building block.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The frame goes together in four parts.",
    "",
    "&a1)&r A 5x5 floor of your building block, with one cap block in its center.",
    "&22)&r Two walls on opposite edges, 3 wide and 3 high, with a &2Magic Wall&r between two building blocks on every layer.",
    "&a3)&r A 5x3 roof across the walls, with the &bAltar Core&r in the center with a building block on each side, a stair on top of each Magic Wall, a row of 3 stairs along each long edge and a cap block on each corner.",
    "&24)&r Four upside-down stairs under the roof, against the inside of the walls.",
    "",
    "Every other block in the 5x5x5 space has to be air. The Compendium's altar page shows the stair directions.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Place a &2Lectern&r on the floor in one corner of an open side, and fix a &aLever&r to the wall at the other end of that same side, one block higher.",
    "",
    "The Spell Recipe goes on the lectern. The lever switches the altar's Etherium draw, which bigger spells need later.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A spell can only be crafted when it has no more distinct ingredients than the altar's power, which is the building block's power plus the cap block's. Use one building block, with its matching stairs, for the whole frame, and one cap type for all five caps.",
    "",
    "- Building blocks give planks 1, stone 2, stone bricks or polished stone 3, &2Witchwood Planks&r, prismarine or quartz 4, nether bricks or polished blackstone 5, end stone bricks or purpur 6.",
    "- Caps give glass 1, iron 4, gold 9, diamond 11, up to a &2Block of Sunstone&r at 15.",
    "",
    "Stone bricks with gold caps give 12, enough for Projectile with Dig. The strongest altar reaches 21.",
  ],
  "quest.7F82B80575A669AE.quest_desc": [
    "You'll need a thunderstorm for this one.",
    "",
    "Summon and defeat the &cLightning Guardian&r. Lay a &2Gold Inlay&r ring, stack two &aCopper Bars&r in its center with a Lightning Rod on top, and wait for lightning to strike the rod.",
    "",
    "Lightning heals it and drowning hurts it. It drops the &2Lightning Charm&r, which pulls nearby items to you while switched on.",
  ],
  "quest.6707C926C50776BD.quest_desc": [
    "Each spell part leans toward one of ten affinities, and casting it pulls you toward that element.",
    "",
    "Cast until you gain your first affinity. A deeper affinity grants passive abilities, and past 50% some of them come with drawbacks.",
    "",
    "Opposite elements push each other down. A fully committed affinity locks in place, and only an &2Affinity Tome&r can move it again.",
  ],
  "quest.5117E5A7B36F61FC.quest_desc": [
    "Every spell the altar builds starts with a &2Blank Rune&r and ends with a &aSpell Parchment&r, and many parts ask for colored runes in between.",
    "",
    "Craft some &aBlank Runes&r. Combine one with any dye for a colored rune; Dig, for example, wants a &2Brown Rune&r.",
    "",
    "A &2Rune Bag&r holds one stack of each color and keeps sixteen colors out of your inventory.",
  ],
  "quest.1F694D7302EBE072.quest_desc": [
    "With the recipe on the lectern, the altar shows the ingredient it wants next, floating above the core.",
    "",
    "Craft your first &aSpell&r. Throw each ingredient into the hollow under the &2Altar Core&r in the order shown, starting with a &aBlank Rune&r and finishing with a Spell Parchment. The spell drops out below the core.",
    "",
    "The first time you use it you choose its icon and name. Casting costs mana, and every successful cast earns magic XP.",
  ],
  "quest.7B5AE868BF763D43.title": "Getting Stronger",
  "quest.2A0AC5FFA464150C.quest_desc": [
    "Magic level 10 is the suggestion for the first guardian.",
    "",
    "Summon and defeat the &cWater Guardian&r. In an ocean, river, beach or swamp biome in the Overworld, lay the &2Redstone Inlay&r ring and drop a &aBoat&r and a Water Bucket in the center.",
    "",
    "It splits into clones that soak up hits, and lightning hurts it most. It drops &2Water Orbs&r, which let you breathe and swim freely underwater.",
  ],
  "quest.7C03B317E26A290C.title": "Ice Guardian",
  "quest.4416B4374B2A0CE5.quest_desc": [
    "A piece of the first guardian calls this one.",
    "",
    "Summon and defeat the &cFire Guardian&r in the Nether. Lay a &2Gold Inlay&r ring on a 3x3 of &aObsidian&r and drop a Water Affinity Essence in the center.",
    "",
    "Fire and freezing do nothing to it, but drowning hurts it. It drops &2Fire Antennae&r, a helmet that makes you immune to fire and lets you swim through lava.",
  ],
  "quest.047392629FC030FF.quest_desc": [
    "Skill points come from leveling your magic, and you level by casting.",
    "",
    "Each successful cast earns magic XP equal to the number of different affinities in the spell, so spells that mix elements level you faster. Continuous spells earn a quarter of that.",
    "",
    "Blue points arrive every level. Green points start at level 10 and come every 2 levels after that, and red points start at level 20 and come every 3 levels.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The Forget All button in the Occulus refunds every point for one &2Block of Vinteum&r.",
  ],
  "quest.6707C926C50776BD.title": "Affinities",
  "quest.4E5672F36E0FBD81.quest_desc": [
    "An obelisk burns fuel. A &dCelestial Prism&r makes light Etherium from the sun, and Beam, Chain and the health contingency accept nothing else.",
    "",
    "Turn an &2Obelisk&r into a &dCelestial Prism&r with the Purification ritual on the next page. The prism only generates during the day, and only while it can see the sky.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Place an obelisk and draw the purification pattern around it in &2Wizard's Chalk&r, with a lit &aCandle&r in each of its four corners; the Compendium shows the exact shape. The space around it has to be clear.",
    "",
    "Drop a &2Moonstone&r within 4 blocks, stand on top of the obelisk and cast a spell that contains both Self and Light. The moonstone is used up and the obelisk becomes the prism.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "On its own a prism makes 1 Etherium every 6 ticks. A chalk ring speeds it up, and pillars on the 5x5 corners speed it up further, until the top tier makes 1 every tick.",
    "",
    "Each pillar is two &2Quartz Pillars&r with a catalyst block on top. The catalyst sets the tier: Chimerite, then gold, diamond and finally &2Sunstone&r blocks.",
  ],
  "quest.1FF93FE18E8F7EE4.quest_desc": [
    "Affinity Tomes turn up in loot chests, each tied to the element of the place it was found, tomes turn up in bastions and fortresses, water in shipwrecks, earth in mineshafts and so on.",
    "",
    "Find an &aAffinity Tome&r. Reading one adds 10% to its affinity and takes 10% from every other, and it is the only way to shift a locked affinity.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The &3Arcanist&r sells them too.",
  ],
  "quest.53E89BAA247F2D81.title": "Wizard's Chalk",
  "quest.2779B1ED12A8A648.quest_desc": [
    "This armor looks after itself.",
    "",
    "Craft the four pieces of &aMage Armor&r. Each takes wool, leather and a rune, and they repair themselves with your mana.",
  ],
  "quest.5E3BBD0F8D9946E3.quest_desc": [
    "Eleven spell parts can't be bought with skill points. They're learned by experiment.",
    "",
    "Learn a silver spell part by casting a spell that contains the right combination of parts. Frost Damage, Frost and Storm together teach &2Blizzard&r, for example. The Compendium's silver spell parts page gives hints for working out the rest.",
    "",
    "Five of them also need an ingot dropped on the ground within 4 blocks of you when you cast. &2Falling Star&r, Blizzard and Fire Rain need an &aAdamantite Ingot&r. Daylight and Moonrise need an &aAeternium Ingot&r. The ingot is used up when the part is learned.",
    "",
    "A silver part still has to be crafted at the altar afterwards, and several of them need a guardian's essence.",
  ],
  "quest.716BACCDE07BB05E.quest_desc": [
    "Links between generators and the altar can't be seen.",
    "",
    "Craft &aMagitech Goggles&r. Worn as a helmet or in a head curio slot, they show every Etherium link, which makes a broken connection easy to spot.",
  ],
  "quest.64FB0BBFC60A0A4D.quest_desc": [
    "Of all the rituals in the book, this one is the darkest.",
    "",
    "Summon and defeat the &cLife Guardian&r. On a new moon in the Overworld, draw a hollow 5x5 square of &2Wizard's Chalk&r with a lit &aCandle&r 1 block outside the middle of each side. A baby villager killed by a player in the center calls it.",
    "",
    "It can't be hurt directly, so kill the minions it summons. It drops the &2Life Ward&r, which keeps a regenerating absorption shield on you while it sits in your inventory.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The Compendium says a full moon, but the ritual checks for a new moon.",
  ],
  "quest.43B8B4ADA8187922.quest_desc": [
    "Three minerals are required through the early game, and all three are mined in the Overworld.",
    "",
    "Mine &aVinteum&r and &2Topaz&r, and dig deeper for Chimerite. Vinteum goes into the Altar Core, Magic Walls and the Obelisk, so collect plenty.",
    "",
    "- &aVinteum Ore&r: Y -16 to 80, and common. &dMana Creepers&r drop the dust too.",
    "- &2Chimerite Ore&r: Y -16 to 16. It drops the gem directly, and Silk Touched ore can't be smelted.",
    "- &aTopaz Ore&r: Y -80 to 80, with extra veins high up in mountains.",
  ],
  "quest.04A54945082F9B5C.title": "Ender Guardian",
  "quest.4416B4374B2A0CE5.title": "Fire Guardian",
  "quest.42CCD46AABFF6DAF.quest_desc": [
    "Summon and defeat the &cArcane Guardian&r.",
    "",
    "Lay an &2Iron Inlay&r ring, and along one side of it place a &aBookshelf&r, an empty Lectern facing the ring and another Bookshelf, with each bookshelf stacked 3 high. Drop an &2Arcane Compendium&r in the center.",
    "",
    "It drops the &2Arcane Spell Book&r, which casts for 20% less mana and makes its spells 40% stronger.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: The ritual uses up the Compendium, so make a spare first.",
  ],
  "quest.1A9736775EA052B0.title": "Guardian Rituals",
  "quest.5EE9E2D553EC2130.title": "Spell Book",
  "quest.45CD833DF80BEAC3.title": "Mana and Burnout",
  "quest.04A54945082F9B5C.quest_desc": [
    "The last guardian waits in the End, and calling it takes a &2Black Aurem&r. The Compendium suggests magic level 100.",
    "",
    "Summon and defeat the &cEnder Guardian&r. In the End, lay a 5x5 floor of &2Coal Blocks&r, put a &aGold Inlay&r ring on it with the Black Aurem in the center and a Fire burning 2 blocks out from the middle of each side, then drop an Eye of Ender into the aurem.",
    "",
    "Magic and drowning hurt it most. Any Enderman that strikes it dies and heals it, so clear them out first. It drops &2Ender Boots&r, which flip your gravity when you jump.",
  ],
  "quest.460216B38525C483.title": "Battlemage Armor",
  "quest.1A9736775EA052B0.quest_desc": [
    "Ten &cGuardians&r stand between you and the strongest magic in the mod. None of them spawn on their own. Nine are called with rituals, and the tenth comes when you anger a forest.",
    "",
    "Craft eight &aRedstone Inlays&r and lay them as a hollow 3x3 ring. That ring is the whole of the Water Guardian's ritual.",
    "",
    "Every guardian drops an &2Affinity Essence&r that unlocks new spell parts, plus an item of its own. An essence can be duplicated with arcane ash and themed items, so one kill is enough.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Most rituals start with a ring of one inlay type: &2Redstone Inlay&r, &aIron Inlay&r or Gold Inlay. A ring is 8 inlays around an empty block, and the trigger item is dropped in that center. Keep the area around a ritual clear, because its empty spaces have to be air.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: In this pack every guardian spawns as an &eApotheosis&r boss with extra affixes, so they hit harder than the Compendium suggests.",
  ],
  "quest.3EB5B2498F0B2A8A.title": "Moonstone",
  "quest.4BDB6F7BD54FE910.quest_desc": [
    "That pool is worth taking. Bathing in Etherium gives Mana Regeneration, and a bucket is the richest fuel an &2Obelisk&r can burn.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: A cauldron holds Liquid Etherium too, if you want a supply near your altar.",
  ],
  "quest.53E89BAA247F2D81.quest_desc": [
    "Chalk marks out every ritual in the mod, from an obelisk's first upgrade to the circle that calls the Life Guardian.",
    "",
    "Craft &aWizard's Chalk&r and draw with it on the ground. A full ring of 8 chalk around an obelisk is its first tier.",
  ],
  "quest.2E24342B5A3D96C7.title": "Earth Guardian",
  "quest.7F82B80575A669AE.title": "Lightning Guardian",
  "quest.5117E5A7B36F61FC.title": "Runes",
  "quest.5EE9E2D553EC2130.quest_desc": [
    "Spells pile up fast once the altar is running.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aSpell Book&r. Sneak + Right-click to open its storage, put spells on its hotbar page and shift-scroll while holding it to switch between them.",
  ],
  "quest.4E5672F36E0FBD81.title": "&dCelestial Prism",
  "quest.2E24342B5A3D96C7.quest_desc": [
    "A plain ring won't call the Earth Guardian.",
    "",
    "Summon and defeat the &cEarth Guardian&r in the Overworld. Its ritual is an &2Iron Inlay&r ring on a 3x3 of &aObsidian&r with Chiseled Stone Bricks under the center, plus a Vinteum Torch 2 blocks out from the middle of each side. Drop an &2Emerald&r, a &aChimerite&r and a Topaz in the center.",
    "",
    "Fire and lightning don't touch it, but drowning and freezing do. It drops &2Earth Armor&r, a chestplate that adds attack damage and makes you immune to fire.",
  ],
  "quest.7935F6FE44D4CFD3.quest_desc": [
    "No ritual calls the Nature Guardian. It comes when you anger the forest.",
    "",
    "Defeat the &cNature Guardian&r. Kill 20 &dDryads&r in a forest within one minute; it appears where the last one fell. Dryads wander in groups of 15 to 25 and follow saplings.",
    "",
    "Fire and freezing hurt it, and drowning heals it. It drops the &2Nature Scythe&r, a heavy weapon that comes back when thrown.",
  ],
  "quest.3EB5B2498F0B2A8A.quest_desc": [
    "Moonstone falls from the sky.",
    "",
    "Find a meteorite and mine &aMoonstone&r. Meteorites are mounds of stone about 5 blocks wide, scattered across dry land above Y 56, and they're rare, about one in every 400 chunks.",
  ],
  "quest.2779B1ED12A8A648.title": "Mage Armor",
  "quest.716BACCDE07BB05E.title": "Magitech Goggles",
  "quest.1A850EA969AFE13C.quest_desc": [
    "Dark Etherium comes from the &dBlack Aurem&r, which drains the life of whatever stands next to it.",
    "",
    "Corrupt an &2Obelisk&r into a &dBlack Aurem&r with the ritual on the next page, then keep living mobs penned within 2 blocks of it. Undead and bosses are immune, and Summon and the death contingency need its dark Etherium.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Draw the corruption pattern around an obelisk in &2Wizard's Chalk&r, with a lit &aCandle&r at each of its four marked spots; the Compendium shows the shape. Drop a &2Sunstone&r within 4 blocks, stand on top of the obelisk and cast a spell with Fire Damage on yourself.",
    "",
    "Its tiers use the same pillars and catalysts as the prism, with &2Nether Bricks&r in place of quartz.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The &dAurem&r forms a block above the ground, and its tier ring wants it at ground level, so you may need to break it and place it again. It drops itself.",
  ],
  "quest.14DC3D850BC8283C.title": "Your First Design",
  "quest.3070FD15982582F5.quest_desc": [
    "Magic in &eArs Magica Legacy&r stays locked until you hold the &aArcane Compendium&r, which has no regular crafting recipe.",
    "",
    "Find a pool of &2Liquid Etherium&r, which form in plains, roughly one in every 50 chunks. Hang an &2Item Frame&r on a wall so the pool sits 2 blocks out in front of it and 1 to 2 blocks lower, then put a plain &aBook&r in the frame. A few seconds later it turns into the &aCompendium&r.",
    "",
    "{image:ftb:textures/quests/ars_magica/ars_book.png width:127 height:100 align:center}",
    "",
    "Picking it up starts you at magic level 1 with 3 blue skill points, and it opens the &3Arcanist&r shop.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Each magic level you gain here also levels the pack's \", {\"text\": \"Magic skill tree\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ftb:skills,ftb:magic.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Skill Trees guide\"}}, \", which is separate from these skill points.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.047392629FC030FF.title": "Skill Points",
  "task.6BD5C23831ED861B.title": "&eObserve&r: &dBlack Aurem",
  "quest.14DC3D850BC8283C.quest_desc": [
    "The Compendium suggests a simple first spell: Projectile with Dig, which breaks blocks at range.",
    "",
    "Write a &aSpell Recipe&r. Put a &2Book and Quill&r in the table, drag Projectile into a shape group and Dig into the Spell Grammar row, then drag the finished book into your inventory.",
    "",
    "Shift-clicking the book out cancels the design, so take it out by hand.",
  ],
  "quest.234EDABC4DC710EC.title": "Air Guardian",
  "quest.7935F6FE44D4CFD3.title": "Nature Guardian",
  "quest.5D40844A4B69B3E8.quest_desc": [
    "Learning a part is half the job. The other half is writing the spell down.",
    "",
    "Craft some &aSpell Parchment&r and an &2Inscription Table&r. The table turns a &2Book and Quill&r into a spell design, and a sheet of parchment is the last ingredient of every spell you build.",
  ],
  "quest.42CCD46AABFF6DAF.title": "Arcane Guardian",
  "quest.3ED3881C36561AFA.title": "The Occulus",
  "quest.4BDB6F7BD54FE910.title": "Liquid Etherium",
  "quest.64FB0BBFC60A0A4D.title": "Life Guardian",
  "quest.7B5AE868BF763D43.quest_desc": [
    "Green skill points don't appear until magic level 10.",
    "",
    "Reach magic level 10 by casting spells. Green points open the stronger half of every tree, and the Compendium suggests level 10 for the first guardian.",
  ],
  "quest.5D40844A4B69B3E8.title": "The Inscription Table",
}